course: dictionary
lesson: 10719
title: Unwashed and what it tells you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «unwashed» is built from two parts you already know: un- means not, and washed means cleaned with water. So unwashed means not washed, and still dirty. When you meet a long word, look for small parts you know.
explain: Look at the sentence: «Food can be dangerous in hidden ways: dirt on unwashed fruit, a food a friend is allergic to, or a whole grape that can block a small child's airway.» The clue is dirt. Unwashed fruit still has dirt on it, so it is not clean enough to eat yet.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in: "dirt on not-washed fruit" still makes sense, so you are right. Unwashed can also describe hands, dishes and clothes. A pile of unwashed dishes in a story might show a messy home.
fact: Unwashed means not washed; still dirty.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unwashed means not washed.
fact: «Unwashed hands» can carry germs, so wash your hands before eating.
fact: «Unwashed fruit and vegetables» should be washed before you eat them.
fact: In a story, «unwashed dishes» can show a messy home.
exercise: «Food can be dangerous in hidden ways: dirt on unwashed fruit, a food a friend is allergic to, or a whole grape that can block a small child's airway.» What does unwashed mean here? | Very old | Cooked and hot | Freshly cleaned and shiny | *Still dirty, not washed
exercise: Rania says «unwashed hands» are clean because they have soap on them. What is wrong with that? | Soap makes hands dirtier | *Unwashed means not washed, so the hands can still carry germs | Hands are only dirty when they are wet | Unwashed hands are always warm
exercise: What does the prefix un- mean in the word unwashed? | Very | Again | Under | *Not
test: «The pile of unwashed dishes sat in the sink for a week.» What does this suggest about the home? | A home by the sea | *A messy home | A new home | A very tidy home
test: Which should be washed before you eat them? | A dry towel | A cup of water | *Unwashed fruit and vegetables | A clean plate
exam: A child says «unwashed clothes» are clean because they are folded neatly. Is she right? | Yes, folding makes clothes clean | Yes, unwashed means freshly ironed | No, unwashed means wet | *No, unwashed means not washed, so they are still dirty
